    "whyItMatters": "The NCE may frame referral as automatically caring or continued treatment as automatically loyal. Both can be wrong. Referral can be discriminatory, premature, passive, or used to escape a difficult client. Continuing can be harmful when the counselor lacks competence or treatment is ineffective. The ethical task is to determine why a change is needed and then create a clinically responsible transition.",
